# HK/US Insider Radar Skill

When the user asks for HK/US insider trading, 港股美股内部人交易, 董监高增减持, insider buying/selling, 内部人净买入, 内部人聚集买入, or an insider-trade radar report, use the local skill package.

Preferred local project path:

```text
.cursor/skills/hk-us-insider-radar
```

Workflow:

1. Read `.cursor/skills/hk-us-insider-radar/SKILL.md`.
2. For routing, the direction/type taxonomy, role weighting, netting rules, cluster detection, report format, empty-data handling, or QA, also read `.cursor/skills/hk-us-insider-radar/references/insider-playbook.md`.
3. Validate generated reports with `.cursor/skills/hk-us-insider-radar/scripts/validate_report.py`.
4. Use the local `pandadata-api` skill for the exact `get_stock_insider_trade` (HK) and `get_stock_insider_transaction` (US) contracts before any real API call.
5. Route by market: `.HK` → `get_stock_insider_trade`, US tickers → `get_stock_insider_transaction`; both share the same field schema.
6. Bucket every transaction (open-market buy/sale vs option/gift/plan); the headline net is **open-market only**. Read direction from the **signed** `adjusted_trade_shares` and `transaction_type` together — never from price or holdings alone.
7. State the filing lag (`info_date` filing ≠ `transaction_date` trade), report value per `currency` (no cross-currency sums), weight principals via `insider_role`/`is_main_role`, and never invent transactions, roles, prices, credentials, or investment advice.
